<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy" %>

<%= render "legal/document", title: "Privacy Policy" do %>
  <p>
    <strong><%= Legal::SERVICE_NAME %></strong> is a self-hosted personal dashboard. This
    installation is run by an individual operator on their own hardware; there is
    no company behind it and no third party operating it on their behalf. This
    policy describes what the software stores and what it does with it.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your account</strong> — email address, an encrypted password hash, and optionally your name, time zone and postal code (used to pick a weather location).</li>
    <li><strong>Credentials for accounts you connect</strong> — OAuth tokens, app passwords and API keys for the services you choose to link. These are encrypted at rest and are never displayed back to you after saving.</li>
    <li><strong>Cached panel data</strong> — the most recent result of each connected service, so the dashboard renders without waiting on a third party. Each refresh replaces the previous copy.</li>
    <li><strong>Things you create here</strong> — todos, countdowns, habits and bookmarks. A habit also keeps the dates you marked it done, which is what the activity graph is drawn from.</li>
    <li><strong>Notification subscriptions</strong> — if you enable push notifications, the browser endpoint needed to deliver them.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage reports you push</strong> — if you install the usage reporter, the token counts and rate-limit figures it sends from your own machines.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not done with it</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is not sold, rented, or shared with anyone. It is not used for
    advertising or profiling, and it is not used to train machine learning
    models. There are no analytics, trackers or third-party scripts on any page
    of this application.
  </p>

  <h2>Data from services you connect</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect an account, this application reads only what the
    corresponding panel needs, using read-only permissions wherever the service
    offers them:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Calendar</strong> — events in your calendars for the current day, to list today's meetings and their video-call links.</li>
    <li><strong>Gmail</strong> — unread message counts and the sender and subject of recent unread messages, to show a mail summary. Message bodies and attachments are not read or stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Slack</strong> — unread conversation counts for the workspaces you connect.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — your notifications and the pull requests awaiting your review.</li>
    <li><strong>IMAP mailboxes</strong> — unread counts and message headers.</li>
    <li><strong>Home Assistant</strong> — camera snapshots, proxied through this server so your cameras are not exposed directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Weather services</strong> — forecasts and alerts for a location you specify.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is fetched only to be displayed on your own dashboard. It is
    stored solely as the cache described above, and is not transferred to anyone
    else.
  </p>

  <h2>Google user data</h2>
  <p>
    <% policy_url = "https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" %>
    Use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <%= link_to "Google API Services User Data Policy", policy_url, rel: "noopener noreferrer", target: "_blank" %>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
    Specifically: Google user data is used only to provide the calendar and mail
    panels you have enabled, is never sold, is never used for advertising, and is
    never read by a human except where you have explicitly asked for support or
    where required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Disconnecting an account deletes its stored credentials and its cached data immediately.</li>
    <li>Deleting your account removes everything associated with it.</li>
    <li>Cached panel data is overwritten on each refresh and is not archived.</li>
    <li>You can revoke this application's access from the service's own settings at any time — for Google, at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Connection credentials are encrypted at rest. All traffic is served over
    HTTPS. Because this is a self-hosted installation, its security also depends
    on the machine it runs on and on the operator who maintains it.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This application is not directed at children under 13 and no account should be created for one.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <% if Legal.contact %>
      Questions about this policy, or requests to see or delete your data, can go to
      <a href="mailto:<%= Legal.contact %>"><%= Legal.contact %></a>.
    <% else %>
      Questions about this policy, or requests to see or delete your data, should
      go to the operator of this installation.
    <% end %>
  </p>
<% end %>
